[31m+ const textureCache = new Map<string, THREE.Texture>();[39m
[31m+[39m
[31m+ /* The renderer's real anisotropy ceiling, captured at scene[39m
[31m+  * construction (overhaul audit T12: the hard-coded 8 smeared the[39m
[31m+  * plaza floor at the grazing angles the world is mostly viewed[39m
[31m+  * from — most current phones/desktops support 16). */[39m
[31m+ let maxTextureAnisotropy = 8;[39m
[31m+[39m
[31m+ /* Stack-100 #2 items 82/84/94 — the rung's anisotropy, applied[39m
[31m+  * honestly everywhere a surface map is born and re-applied on every[39m
[31m+  * ladder step. Two facts used to break the ladder's word: textures[39m
[31m+  * were created at the DEVICE ceiling (a low-rung scene still decoded[39m
[31m+  * its surfaces at anisotropy 16 until some later step happened to[39m
[31m+  * re-range the colour cache), and the derived PBR sets + brushed[39m
[31m+  * gold maps were never re-ranged at all — the tier pass iterated the[39m
[31m+  * colour textureCache only, so the maps that carry the palace's[39m
